---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import Link from '@/components/Link.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <PageHead slot="head" title="Projects" />
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[{ label: 'Projects', href: '/projects', icon: 'lucide:code-2' }]}
  />

  <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h2>
      Current —{' '}
      <Link href="https://computervision.vision" underline>
        computervision.vision
      </Link>
    </h2>
    <p>
      Independent research and deployed tools for seeing inside and steering
      visual models.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://dinodreamer.computervision.vision" underline>
          DinoDreamer
        </Link>{' '}
        — Interactive browser tool for visualizing Meta’s DINOv3. Trained a
        16,384-group Grassmannian block-sparse featurizer and built a Rust/Burn
        to WebAssembly/WebGPU engine so anyone can train and interact with
        neural cellular automata on their own GPU.{' '}
        <span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          (
          <Link
            href="https://computervision.vision/writing/dinodreamer/"
            underline
          >
            Write-up
          </Link>
          {' · '}
          <Link href="https://dinodreamer.computervision.vision" underline>
            Open DinoDreamer
          </Link>
          {' · '}
          <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/dinodreamer" underline>
            Code
          </Link>
          {' · 2026–present'})
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link href="/blog/letting-computers-dance" underline>
          Latent Dance
        </Link>{' '}
        — Real-time music visualizer that steers SDXL through 20,480 sparse
        autoencoder features on a single consumer GPU, turning diffusion into a
        live audio-reactive control loop instead of offline batch generation.{' '}
        <span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          (
          <Link href="/blog/letting-computers-dance" underline>
            Write-up
          </Link>
          {' · '}
          <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/latent-dance" underline>
            Code
          </Link>
          {' · 2025–present'})
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Superseded ideas</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <Link href="/blog/subspacelens" underline>
          SubspaceLens
        </Link>{' '}
        — Measuring subspace geometry in diffusion transformers with MCR² coding
        rates instead of sparse autoencoders. Superseded once I moved away from
        generative decoders toward representation models and DinoDreamer, kept
        here as the detour that got me there.{' '}
        <span class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          (
          <Link href="/blog/subspacelens" underline>
            Write-up
          </Link>
          {' · '}
          <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/SubspaceLens" underline>
            Code
          </Link>
          {' · 2026'})
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Past</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/SAM_CAM_BAM" underline>
          SAM_CAM_BAM
        </Link>{' '}
        — Live Rust music visualizer pairing ONNX webcam segmentation with
        real-time audio frequency analysis. (2025)
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/hambaJubaTuba" underline>
          hambaJubaTuba
        </Link>{' '}
        — Audio-driven latent trajectories for temporally coherent diffusion
        music visualization; the predecessor to Latent Dance. (2024)
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/better_spotify" underline>
          Better Spotify
        </Link>{' '}
        — Full-stack Rust web app for true random shuffling on Spotify
        playlists. (2025)
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://github.com/hammamiomar/workTimerPet" underline>
          workTimerPet
        </Link>{' '}
        — Work and break timer pet, also living at the bottom of the home page.
        (2025)
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link
          href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ekjcFVN1Jq6dJ0ETpsyNm2pUHbrF-pYx/view?usp=share_link"
          underline
        >
          A Careful Look into Graph Contrastive Learning
        </Link>{' '}
        — Empirical tests of claims in graph contrastive learning. (2022)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Publications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <Link href="https://rosap.ntl.bts.gov/view/dot/72518" underline>
          “Exploring Cost-Effective Computer Vision Solutions for Smart
          Transportation Systems”
        </Link>{' '}
        — USDOT / C2SMART Center (2023)
      </li>
      <li>
        <Link
          href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0965856422001458"
          underline
        >
          “A New Curb Lane Monitoring and Illegal Parking Impact Estimation
          Approach”
        </Link>{' '}
        — Transportation Research Part A (2022)
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
